229	01010000A0E6100000C8CBE63226FF38C0C5D7932DD7E330400000000000000000	237	Las Palmas - Mindelo, Day 8	boat	Sat, 09 Mar 2024 23:00:00 GMT	Marc, Rob, Matty, Rika	We arrived. We made it, we are safe. It was a hell of a trip in the end. First of all the wind slowed down and we took much longer than anticipated. Then when we tried to call the Marina, which via Email agreed to help us, but they didn’t answer. We were making circles in the bay and trying to reach anyone who could help us. We had just one sail, no electricity and no engine so we needed to be towed to a safe harbor. In the end we called 112 and a nice police guy started to organize help. It tool around 2 hours and almost running against a cliff until finally some people in a motor boat arrived and circled the boat. Communication was very difficult, they barely spoke English and we didn’t speak Portuguese. When all the wind died down they finally threw us a rope and started towing. But instead to the Marine they brought us to a massive industrial dock and during the process of docking we almost crashed. There was a lot of shouting and screaming and there were around 5 police men waiting for us. When we finally secured the boat, I immediately fell into a deep sleep.  The next morning I woke up after just 5h and couldn’t go back to sleep anymore. I made myself some scrambled eggs and enjoyed sitting on land. Then I went to search some wifi, found it in a nearby bar and immediately called my mom. The first thing I saw was her worried expression because she didn’t expected to hear from me for another two weeks! Hearing her voice suddenly made me quite emotional and all of a sudden I started to cry. It felt good to release some pressure.	boat	SY Thinking of Dave	1	sleep	\N	\N
