1989	01010000A0E610000008A9CEDBDC1952C091F5289A2FFD45C00000000000000000	2017	La Junta	car	Fri, 06 Mar 2026 23:03:00 GMT	Angelica, Angel	A grandma with her nephew. But she is very young, around 50 and also does not feel like a grandma. She talks like a young person, also by the words she uses. She says most her her friends are the age of her daughter, around 30, they also go partying together. She used to work in a disco for many years, working from 22 to 6 in the morning, while having 4 kids. She lost 8 family members in the landslide of Villa Santa Lucia, including her mom. It was a crazy story and must have been so hard, she just accidentally wasn’t home and went to Futalefu, and when whe returned, half the village was gone. Her mom had a cafeteria and many travelers passed through there. When she died, she got condolences from all over the world. When we drove through Santa Lucia, she showed us where her house used to be. She has 8 butterflies tattooed on her hand, which represents the 8 people she lost. Villa Santa Lucia is named after the wife of Pinochet. Angelica met her and also Pinochet when she was young. She spoke really fondly of him, called him a simple man, a just and honest man. She said that he killed no one. But later she relativated that of course his orders killed people, but not himself. And she said that she likes to focus on the good things he did, like the carretera austral and the fact that there was almost no deliquencia when he was in power. 	\N	\N	1	waypoint	\N	\N
