2162	01010000A0E61000007F79E2E89BBE5DC0E79D41DA2B6B49400000000000000000	2190	Sicamous	car	Thu, 14 May 2026 22:04:00 GMT	Braden	 A dad going to see his kids who live with the mom in Nanaimo. He’s a farm boy, from the prairie and a bit of a simple man, but kind. But I was doubting that his complaining about his wife being crazy is really true. But he always tried to find a silver lining in things, his kids live so far away and he drives out there every month for around a week to see him. Even tho it’s a long drive he is happy to see the coast and get out of home a bit. Also one year ago his house burned down, and he was just happy that no one got hurt and that he had a lodge to sleep in at night. He is torn now to be with his kids and to carry on the family farm, because there is no one else. He gave me chewing tobacco to try out, was pretty gross. 	\N	\N	1	waypoint	\N	\N
2163	01010000A0E610000071B91AA187DE5DC0E82C8FAA05F148400000000000000000	2191	Kelowna	car	Thu, 14 May 2026 22:05:00 GMT	Richelle	When she stopped, the first thing she said was: “I’m a mom, don’t murder me” She was a bit scared and unsure of really doing this. But we quickly got comfortable and had a nice talk. She has a teenage son and is a single mom. She seems to be doing an amazing job, and also has her own life next to it. She has a company for organizing sport events. She used to do triathlons and stuff. She was on her way to Kelowna to have a biking weekend with a friend. She told me the story how recently she went to the States to see her parents, and the border officer asked her where she was going. She said to see her parents, and he asked: Why? She was so taken aback from this question and said: Because I love them. They kept being suspicious and asked her again. It’s crazy what is happening now in the US. 	\N	\N	1	waypoint	\N	\N
